# linked_anim_graph_layer_sample_authoring Design

Date: 2026-06-27
Updated: 2026-06-29

Status: Linked Anim Graph MVP implemented as
`ensure_linked_anim_graph_sample_variant`. Planner/job-contract routing now
recognizes simple sample/temp Linked Anim Graph requests with an existing
compatible linked AnimBP. Linked Anim Layer/interface creation, Sub Anim
Instance compatibility wrappers, and arbitrary graph insertion remain Ieta
design only.

Scope: editor-only, sample-only Linked Anim Graph and Linked Anim Layer
authoring. Runtime/gameplay code and original asset mutation are out of scope.

## Purpose

`ensure_linked_anim_graph_layer_sample_variant` is a proposed guarded design
area for requests that need sample AnimBP modular composition with Linked Anim
Graph, Linked Anim Layer, or the legacy Sub Anim Instance surface.

The first implementation does not cover the whole feature family. MVP supports
one narrow route:

- duplicate or reuse a sample AnimBP under `/Game/_MCP_Sample/` or
  `/Game/_MCP_Temp/`;
- insert a `UAnimGraphNode_LinkedAnimGraph` that points to an existing linked
  AnimBP class with a compatible skeleton;
- build a simple output-to-root chain, plus input-pose-to-linked-graph when
  the linked class exposes a pose input pin;
- compile and read back the linked node settings and topology.

The automatic authoring planner maps simple requests such as "create a sample
Animation Blueprint linked anim graph using an existing compatible linked
AnimBP" to this MVP and keeps linked layer/interface/Sub Anim Instance wording
out of the safe route.

Linked Anim Layer support should be a later increment unless the user supplies
an existing Anim Layer Interface and layer name. Creating interfaces, layer
override graphs, linked input poses, and linked layer nodes in one command is
too broad for a first pass.

## Ieta Review

Request class: create a safe sample modular AnimBP composition using Linked
Anim Graph, Linked Anim Layer, or Sub Anim Instance style nodes.

Existing routes checked:

- `inspect_anim_graph_protected_topology` can read linked nodes when they
  already exist.
- `inspect_anim_graph_node_settings` can read reflected linked node settings
  when supported.
- `create_anim_blueprint_sample` can create a setup AnimBP target but does not
  author linked graph nodes.
- `ensure_anim_state_machine_sample_variant` and ControlRig sample commands do
  not cover linked AnimBP composition.

Why existing routes are insufficient: they do not safely create linked graph or
linked layer nodes, set their target class or interface/layer, allocate linked
input pose pins, and compile/read back the result.

Asset mutation boundary: source AnimBPs, Anim Layer Interfaces, Skeletons, and
animation assets are read-only. The command may modify only target sample assets
under `/Game/_MCP_Sample/` or `/Game/_MCP_Temp/`.

Proposed command family:

- MVP: `ensure_linked_anim_graph_sample_variant`
- Later: `ensure_linked_anim_layer_sample_variant`
- Combined docs label: `ensure_linked_anim_graph_layer_sample_variant`

Default safety guard: require source and linked AnimBP assets to have compatible
Skeletons, require target sample path, reject original asset mutation, and
return `unsupported_feature` for interface/layer creation in MVP.

Approval needed before Tivret implementation: completed for the Linked Anim
Graph MVP. Further C++/API expansion still needs Ieta review before Linked Anim
Layer/interface creation, Sub Anim Instance wrappers, or arbitrary graph
insertion.

## UE 5.6 API Anchors

Use installed UE 5.6 headers as local truth:

| Need | UE 5.6 anchor | Safe access rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Linked Anim Graph editor node | `Engine/Source/Editor/AnimGraph/Public/AnimGraphNode_LinkedAnimGraph.h` | Use `UAnimGraphNode_LinkedAnimGraph` and its `FAnimNode_LinkedAnimGraph Node` member. |
| Linked Anim Graph base | `Engine/Source/Editor/AnimGraph/Public/AnimGraphNode_LinkedAnimGraphBase.h` | Respect `AllocatePoseLinks()`, custom pins, filtering, and loop validation. |
| Linked Anim Graph runtime node | `Engine/Source/Runtime/Engine/Classes/Animation/AnimNode_LinkedAnimGraph.h` | Set `InstanceClass` to a compatible `UAnimInstance` subclass; do not mutate runtime instances. |
| Linked Anim Layer editor node | `Engine/Source/Editor/AnimGraph/Public/AnimGraphNode_LinkedAnimLayer.h` | Use only with an existing interface and valid layer; call layer setup/update helpers where accessible. |
| Linked Anim Layer runtime node | `Engine/Source/Runtime/Engine/Classes/Animation/AnimNode_LinkedAnimLayer.h` | Validate `Interface` and `Layer`; do not manage live linked layer instances. |
| Linked input pose editor node | `Engine/Source/Editor/AnimGraph/Public/AnimGraphNode_LinkedInputPose.h` | Let compiler/schema logic create or validate input pose nodes; do not hand-edit arrays blindly. |
| Linked input pose runtime node | `Engine/Source/Runtime/Engine/Classes/Animation/AnimNode_LinkedInputPose.h` | Treat dynamic links as runtime behavior, not editor proof. |
| Animation graph schema | `Engine/Source/Editor/AnimGraph/Public/AnimationGraphSchema.h` | Use schema-compatible node creation and link behavior. |
| Anim Layer Interface | `Engine/Source/Runtime/Engine/Classes/Animation/AnimLayerInterface.h` and `UAnimLayerInterfaceFactory` | Interface creation is a separate higher-risk task. |
| Linked graph compiler extensions | `Engine/Source/Editor/AnimGraph/Private/AnimBlueprintExtension_LinkedAnimGraph.h`, `AnimBlueprintExtension_LinkedInputPose.h` | Compile/readback must confirm extension-generated mappings rather than assuming pins. |

## Command Schema

Proposed MVP input fields for `ensure_linked_anim_graph_sample_variant`:

| Field | Type | Default | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `source_anim_bp_path` | string | required | Existing AnimBP to duplicate or use as sample template. |
| `linked_anim_bp_path` | string | required | Existing AnimBP whose generated class becomes `InstanceClass`. |
| `target_anim_bp_path` | string | required | Must be under `/Game/_MCP_Sample/` or `/Game/_MCP_Temp/`. |
| `insert_mode` | enum | `input_pose_to_linked_graph_to_root` | MVP should support only one small sample chain. |
| `allow_existing_target_reuse` | bool | `true` | Reuse target under sample/temp root. |
| `replace_existing_sample_graph` | bool | `false` | Replace only supported sample chain. |
| `compile` | bool | `true` | Compile after mutation. |
| `save_asset` | bool | `false` | Save only the target sample asset. |
| `dry_run` | bool | `false` | Resolve and validate without mutation. |

Future input fields for linked layer support:

| Field | Type | Default | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `anim_layer_interface_path` | string | required for layer route | Existing interface only in first layer pass. |
| `layer_name` | string | required for layer route | Must resolve to an existing layer. |
| `linked_layer_instance_bp_path` | string | optional | Existing AnimBP implementing the interface. |

## Response Schema

Return structured evidence:

| Field | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `success` | Whether the sample command completed. |
| `dry_run` | Whether mutation was skipped. |
| `source_anim_bp_path` | Source AnimBP path. |
| `linked_anim_bp_path` | Linked target AnimBP path. |
| `target_anim_bp_path` | Target sample AnimBP path. |
| `source_modified` | Must be false. |
| `linked_source_modified` | Must be false. |
| `target_modified` | True only when dry run is false and target changed. |
| `linked_instance_class` | Resolved generated class used by the linked graph node. |
| `created_node_id` | Linked node GUID. |
| `created_links` | Pose-link summary. |
| `linked_input_pose_summary` | Input pose names and generated pins when available. |
| `compile_result` | Compile status, warnings, and errors. |
| `readback` | Topology/settings summary. |
| `warnings` | Skeleton mismatch, unsupported layer route, loop risk, or skipped detail. |

## Guardrails

Forbidden patterns:

- modifying source AnimBPs, linked AnimBPs, interfaces, Skeletons, or animation
  assets;
- writing outside sample/temp roots;
- creating Anim Layer Interfaces in the linked graph MVP;
- creating linked layer nodes without an existing interface and layer name;
- hand-editing `InputPoses`, `InputPoseNames`, or linked input pose arrays
  without compiler/schema reconciliation;
- ignoring skeleton compatibility or linked-instance loop validation;
- managing live linked instances or calling runtime linking APIs as editor
  authoring proof;
- claiming modular AnimBP runtime behavior without compile/readback and, when
  requested, a separate runtime probe.

## Verification

Docs-only verification for this design:

- `git diff --check`
- Markdown link and trailing-whitespace sanity checks.

Future implementation verification:

1. `dry_run=true` resolves source, linked, and target assets and validates
   Skeleton compatibility without dirtying packages.
2. Create or reuse a target sample AnimBP and insert one linked graph node.
3. Compile and read back `InstanceClass`, pose links, and output link.
4. Confirm source and linked AnimBPs are not dirty.
5. Reject a target path outside sample/temp roots.
6. Reject incompatible Skeletons with a structured error.
7. For later linked layer support, verify the interface and layer name exist
   before creating any node.

## Tivret instruction

For any further expansion from this design, Tivret should:

- keep the implemented Linked Anim Graph MVP as the baseline before linked
  layer authoring;
- keep all writes sample-only and editor-only;
- add or change Python wrappers and server registration only after each C++
  command schema is stable;
- document linked graph and linked layer limits in `Docs/Tools/node_tools.md`;
- avoid creating Anim Layer Interfaces, live linked instances, runtime code,
  gameplay dependencies, or original asset mutation without a new review pass;
- verify dry-run, skeleton compatibility, compile/readback, existing-target
  behavior, and no-dirty-source behavior.
